|~ `::snippet`, the kind of a snippet, and the laws declared under it.
   ~|

:snippet
  |~~ The kind of a snippet, a query a page shows its reader to run and
      see, written in the prose of a doc as a quote under `::snippet`:
      the words of a kind, ::snippet~(::vec | manifest), or a form at
      work, ::snippet~({:a [5 6]} | /a/-1). A law answers true and a
      link opens a page; a snippet answers whatever it shows, which
      `open` runs, and `snippets` reads the snippets of a doc. A snippet
      reproduces a situation for its reader, so it may answer an error,
      and it reads as code.
      ::link~(::link | doc) ::link~(::qlang/hypertext | doc)
  ~~|

:snippet/opensToWhatItShows
  |~~ A snippet opens to what it shows. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ ::snippet~(::vec | manifest) ~~| | snippets | first | open | has ::vec/count)
